{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And the garments of the serad.</b> The garments of transport, with which they cover the ark and the table and the altar and the menorah. And so it is explicit: \"of the tekhelet and the argaman and the worm of scarlet\" (below, 39:1), each one separately, as written in the section of Numbers Sinai: they made garments of serad, and afterward it is written, \"and they made the garments of the holy\" (there, there), and afterward it specified them. Now, the word serad is from the root of fugitive and survivor (Jeremiah 44:14)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra signals the cross-reference to Numbers chapter 4 (parashat Bamidbar Sinai) by the phrase 'there, there' (שם שם), meaning two successive verses in that same passage."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:39:34.892000127Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}